{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791430049,"nonce":"xR0H8lU/NoNOH9lL8cHBVLOK5bQ=","title":"Reflection enum helpers select a symbol from Dynamic type mappings","message":"TestReflect compares Type.typeof(v) against an expected ValueType through Type.enumEq. Emitted MIR passes hidden enum ID 531934586, the deterministic hash of enum:haxe.macro.Type, rather than 411938711 for enum:ValueType. This affects the typeof assertion group.\n\nThe native-valid EnumReflection.hx reproducer imports haxe.macro.Context, then checks typeof values against ValueType variants. Native Haxe reports CONFORMANCE_OK; pinned Cranelift throws \"enum identity\". Evidence: /tmp/rayzor-enum-reflection-native-v1.log and /tmp/rayzor-enum-reflection-before-v1.log. MIR: /tmp/rayzor-reflect-mir-895.log, function unit.TestReflect.typeof.\n\nresolve_enum_symbol currently consults the SymbolTable TypeId-to-symbol map before the actual TypeKind, including shared Dynamic types. Enum helpers should derive identity from a concrete enum type or its alias/generic/nullable wrappers, and not infer an enum from Dynamic or a primitive. Prototype validation is pending.","files":null}]}